bodyguard-of-bits (0.6.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * First hardening release on the v0.6.x branch. Deep-audit
    sub-agent surfaced 14 findings (0 critical + 6 important
    + 8 minor); 6 important + 4 minor shipped.
  * I-1 + atomic-write contract consolidation: extracted
    bob/_atomic.py::atomic_write(path, content, *, mode=) as
    single source of truth; migrated 5 hand-rolled
    implementations (bob/config.py x2, bob/compare.py,
    bob/history.py, bob/recurrence.py); fixed 4 non-atomic
    sites (bob/cron/_install.py, bob/tui/cron.py install
    paths, bob/ignore.py, bob/history.py first-write).
    bob/cron/_io.py::_atomic_write kept as backwards-compat
    alias for test patch target.
  * I-2 EOF contract completion: new bob/_tty.safe_input()
    wrapper + prompt_wizard() now catches EOFError. 11 bare
    input() sites migrated (cron/_install.py x5,
    cron/_manage.py x5, fixes.py x1). Ctrl-D no longer
    crashes any plain-text wizard.
  * I-3 _validate_cron_field step bounds: rejects step values
    exceeding field range (*/200 for minute 0-59 was accepted
    pre-fix; cron then interpreted as "every 200 minutes" =
    never fires).
  * I-4 shlex.quote() applied to 8 cmd=f"..." sites in
    bob/checks/ssh/_subchecks.py (4) + bob/checks/file_perms.py
    (3) + bob/checks/firmware.py (1) where paths could contain
    spaces (from pwd.getpwnam(SUDO_USER).pw_dir, filesystem
    scans, dpkg-query). Pre-fix --fix --apply would chmod the
    wrong file.
  * I-5 history.jsonl mode 0o600 on first write (was inheriting
    process umask, typically 0o644 → world-readable score
    timestamps). os.open(O_WRONLY | O_APPEND | O_CREAT, 0o600)
    sets mode only at creation; existing-file mode preserved.
  * I-6 ignore.py: ignore.yml writes now go through atomic_write.
    Pre-fix raw os.open(O_TRUNC) corrupted on power-loss.
  * M-2: redundant double-.lower() in _apply_bad_directive.
  * M-3: MaxAuthTries=-1 / =0 now treated as default 6 (sshd
    treats <=0 as misconfiguration).
  * M-6: bob/__main__.py fatal-error handler hints
    BOB_DEBUG=1 and prints traceback when set.
  * M-8: --watch=N error wording: "positive integer" →
    "integer ≥ 10" (matches the actual constraint).
  * 4 minor findings deferred (M-1 silent downgrade,
    M-4 documented intentional, M-5 transitively fixed,
    M-7 judgment call).
  * +17 regression tests in tests/test_atomic_v061.py (12) +
    tests/test_cron.py::TestStepBoundedToFieldRange (5).
  * 4583 → 4600 tests.
  * JSON contract (schema_version="1"), 116 EXPLAIN_KEYS,
    keybindings, no-curses fallback, exit codes — all
    preserved.
  * Wire output unchanged. Only --watch=N error string differs.
  * Two contracts now uniformly enforced across the codebase:
    atomic-write (every persistent write goes through
    _atomic.atomic_write) and EOF handling (every interactive
    read site routes Ctrl-D to clean exit).

