bodyguard-of-bits (0.6.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Major bump opening the v0.6.x branch. Two architectural
    splits (#13 + #14) deliberately deferred across the entire
    v0.5.x cycle, plus one sunset honored. All changes
    contract-preserving via package __init__.py re-exports —
    every `from bob.checks.ssh import …` or
    `from bob.cron import …` call site continues to work
    unchanged.
  * #13 — bob/checks/ssh.py (1296 LoC monolith) → bob/checks/ssh/
    package with 4 submodules:
      _directives.py (165L): _BadDirective table +
        _BAD_DIRECTIVES tuple + _apply_bad_directive helper +
        weak crypto reference sets (_WEAK_CIPHERS, _WEAK_MACS,
        _WEAK_KEX).
      _snapshot.py (198L): 5 dataclasses + SSHSnapshot +
        SSHSnapshot.from_system. Uses function-local
        `from . import _parsers` to break the natural cycle
        with the parser layer.
      _parsers.py (446L): all pure parsers — sshd_config,
        authorized_keys, known_hosts, client config — plus
        key-type/RSA-bits helpers + _collect_host_keys +
        _detect_ssh_install_cmd + _parse_time_seconds.
      _subchecks.py (529L): check_ssh entry point + all
        _check_* per-area helpers.
  * #14 — bob/cron.py (1204 LoC monolith) → bob/cron/ package
    with 4 submodules:
      _parse.py (330L): CronEntry + parse_cron_file +
        list_installed_crons + cron_to_human +
        build_schedule_expr + validators + day helpers + MTA
        detection + constants.
      _io.py (164L): _atomic_write + build_script_content +
        apply_cron_schedule + apply_cron_email.
      _install.py (319L): prompt_emails / prompt_email +
        _run_install_cron_plain + run_install_cron +
        _CronQuit exception (shared with _manage).
      _manage.py (445L): _manage_email_store +
        edit_cron_email + edit_cron_schedule +
        _run_manage_cron_plain + run_manage_cron.
  * Sunset: UFW_AUDIT_SHARE legacy env var removed. Announced
    "REMOVED in v0.6.0" in the v0.5.4 deprecation warning. Only
    BOB_SHARE is now accepted by resolve_share_dir(). Installers
    still setting UFW_AUDIT_SHARE will see no effect — update
    them to use BOB_SHARE.
  * Test infrastructure updates (3 trivial fixes, mechanical
    only — coverage unchanged):
      tests/test_template_vars_migration.py: _check_modules →
        _module_paths handles both files and package dirs;
        pilot list converted from .py-suffixed to module-name.
      tests/test_domain_scores_mapping_complete.py: glob →
        rglob with __pycache__ filter so the AST scanner
        picks up bob/checks/ssh/_subchecks.py.
      tests/test_cron.py::TestApplyCronScheduleAtomic: spy
        target shifted from bob.cron._atomic_write to
        bob.cron._io._atomic_write (where apply_cron_schedule
        now lives + calls it).
  * 4583 tests inchangés (0 added, 0 removed — splits +
    sunset are wire-equivalent).
  * Largest module post-split is ssh/_subchecks.py at 529L,
    well below the project's soft 1000-LoC ceiling.
  * JSON contract (schema_version="1"), 116 EXPLAIN_KEYS,
    keybindings, no-curses fallback, exit codes — all
    preserved.
  * Backwards compatibility: every public symbol from v0.5.x
    monoliths is re-exported by the new packages'
    __init__.py. Zero user-visible import breakage.
  * Closes the deferred architectural roadmap from v0.5.x.
  * Next: v0.6.x maintenance + cross-distro field bug reports.
    No deep-audit campaign planned (v0.5.x closed
    comprehensively: 25 modules deep-audited + ~25
    spot-checked, 0 critical findings outstanding).

