bodyguard-of-bits (0.5.7-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=low

  * Targeted hardening pass on curses TUI: bob/manage_logs.py
    (999 LoC) and bob/tui/cron.py (920 LoC) — the bucket
    explicitly deferred by the v0.5.5 and v0.5.6 audits.
    11 findings from a focused sub-agent: 0 critical, 3
    important, 8 minor (3 shipped + 5 deferred to v0.5.8).
  * I-1 — _curses_readline accepted curses KEY_* keypad codes
    as input characters via chr(ch_i). Pressing arrows or
    function keys inserted Greek/Unicode glyphs (KEY_UP=259
    → chr(259) = 'Ι', KEY_F1=265 → chr(265) = 'Ω') into
    name/email/days/time/custom-expression input buffers.
    No security impact thanks to downstream validation
    (_EMAIL_RE, _validate_custom_cron, digit-only filter,
    make_slug whitelist) but UX-visibly corrupted. Fix:
    new _is_printable_input_char(ch_i) helper bounds inputs
    to printable Latin-1 only (32 <= ch_i < 256 and isprintable).
  * I-2 — three bare input() sites in manage_logs.py did not
    catch EOFError. Ctrl-D at the path prompt, the move-logs
    [y/N] confirmation, or the delete-all [y/N] confirmation
    dumped a Python traceback. Fix: try/except EOFError on
    all three sites matching the _rl() convention — EOF
    treated as empty input (falls through to "use default"
    for paths, "no" for confirmations). KeyboardInterrupt
    propagates naturally (Python's exit-130 default).
  * I-3 — apply_cron_schedule() used raw os.open(O_WRONLY |
    O_CREAT | O_TRUNC) + fdopen.write instead of the project's
    _atomic_write helper. Power-loss or SIGKILL between
    open(O_TRUNC) and write would leave the cron file empty
    → cron silently drops the entry. Asymmetric with the
    sister apply_cron_email which already used _atomic_write
    (since v0.5.5 #C-1). Fix: switch to _atomic_write(path,
    new_text, mode=0o640) — mode preserved (cron skips
    files with wrong mode).
  * M-1 — manage_logs.deleted_one status flashed
    pending_delete[0].name even when index 0 failed to
    unlink (permission denied) and only a different index
    succeeded. Now tracks the first successfully-deleted
    name explicitly.
  * M-3 — dead-code elif body in _curses_edit_sub
    (chosen = sel; if ch_i == ord("1"): chosen = 0; elif
    ord("2"): chosen = 1 — guard already constrained
    chosen == sel). Simplified, elif rewritten with
    explicit parentheses.
  * M-4 — duplicate `from bob.cron import apply_cron_schedule,
    apply_cron_email` at line 132 consolidated into the
    main import block.
  * Deferred to v0.5.8 (5 cosmetic minors): M-2 cursor-shift
    assumes deletions sit before cursor, M-5 schedule wizard
    local constants → module-level IntEnum, M-6 summary_start
    falsy check misses index 0 (unreachable), M-7 over-greedy
    continuation grouping in _extract_summary_view, M-8
    local `from datetime import` lifted to module top.
  * +11 regression tests across tests/test_cron.py
    (TestApplyCronScheduleAtomic, TestIsPrintableInputChar)
    and tests/test_manage_logs.py (TestEOFErrorOnPromptPath,
    TestEOFErrorOnMoveConfirm, TestEOFErrorOnDeleteAllConfirm,
    TestDeletedOneCorrectName).
  * 4560 → 4571 tests.
  * Single-commit release. JSON contract (schema_version="1"),
    116 EXPLAIN_KEYS, keybindings, no-curses fallback path,
    exit codes — all preserved.
  * UX-visible deltas only: clean Ctrl-D exit (no traceback),
    arrow/function keys no longer print Greek glyphs in TUI
    prompts.
  * After v0.5.7, v0.5.x deep-audit campaign closed:
    25 modules audited + ~25 spot-checked. v0.5.8 will clear
    the 5 deferred cosmetic minors. v0.6.0 reserved for #13
    (ssh.py split) + #14 (cron.py split).

